        <headline>Coastal Flood Advisory issued September 25 at 4:43PM EDT until September 25 at 10:00PM EDT by NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Up to one half foot of inundation above ground level in
low lying areas due to tidal flooding.

* WHERE...Shoreline in the City of Alexandria and Arlington
County.

* WHEN...Until 10 PM EDT this evening, especially around the
time of high tide.

* IMPACTS...Water is expected to approach the curb near the
intersection of King Street and Strand Street in Alexandria.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Tides one to one and a half feet above
normal. The next high tide at Alexandria is at 8:21 PM.
</description>
        <instruction>If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be
closed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of
unknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone
property.</instruction>
